    "Shape estimated as a box for 19 part(s): BUS1, CV1, L6, Q1, Q2, Q3, U8, U9, U12, U13, U14, U15 .... Their fit can't be guaranteed: add a 3D model, set jig.heights, or leave them out with jig.ignore.",
    "Pockets follow each part's 3D shape; a hold pocket's floor is the part's own top, so every part touches its pocket as the board lands (jig.hold_depth_offset_mm +0.00 mm).",
    "Heat: P1, P2, P3, P8 get hot all over while they are soldered (metal body (bnc); pin 2 on GND: a big pin (1.5 mm drill)). Their pockets have 1.0 mm of room all round: line each with 1.0 mm of heat-resistant material (silicone sheet, PTFE, FR-4) before the part goes in, so the hot part never touches the print (jig.heat_insert_mm, jig.hot_parts).",
    "Two-jig workflow: put the PCB top side up in the placement jig, fit the parts, put this holding jig on top (pockets down), turn the stack over, lift off the placement jig and solder from above.",
    "Fit check (189 parts, their 3D shapes): nothing touches on the way in; all 45 hand-soldered parts touch their pockets (or their inserts) as the board lands on the support (within 0.01 mm) and are held on all four sides (0.19 to 0.41 mm of play, inserts in place); held by the part beside it, too close for a jig wall between them: L6 -x against J4 (0.19 mm), U15 -y against U17 (0.68 mm), U17 +y against U15 (0.68 mm); room for inserts: P1 1.0 mm, P2 1.0 mm, P3 1.0 mm, P8 1.0 mm; the holding jig closes over the placement jig without touching it. Estimated (box) shapes: BUS1, CV1, L6, Q1, Q2, Q3, U8, U9, U12, U13."
